# Copy to .env at the repository root. The BFF reads this; the browser never does.
#
# NOTE: OIDC_CLIENT_* is a single SHARED service account (nictiz-ui-svc in the
# freshehr Keycloak realm). The BFF applies no per-user access control, so
# anyone who can reach it can read and write every record. See the Security
# section of the README before deploying anything.

EHRBASE_BASE=http://localhost:8082/ehrbase/rest/openehr/v1

# Keycloak client_credentials for the BFF→EHRbase hop. These are the fixed dev
# values that `npm run register` installs into the local realm (the stack's
# committed realm import carries only its own infrastructure clients — this
# app registers its clients itself). Changing them here without re-running
# `npm run register` breaks every EHRbase call with a token error.
OIDC_TOKEN_URL=http://localhost:8081/auth/realms/freshehr/protocol/openid-connect/token
OIDC_CLIENT_ID=nictiz-ui-svc
OIDC_CLIENT_SECRET=dev-nictiz-ui-svc-secret

FHIR_BASE=http://localhost:8080/fhir

# openFHIR (FHIR Connect mapping engine). Server-side only: every call goes
# through the BFF, which authenticates as nictiz-ui-svc with scope
# openfhir.map — the engine is an OAuth2 resource server (openfhir.protected
# in the stack); `npm run register` attaches the scope + tenant mapper.
OPENFHIR_BASE=http://localhost:8083

# BFF port, and the origin the Vite dev server is served from.
PORT=3001
CORS_ORIGIN=http://localhost:5173

# ── Deployment-only settings ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
# All of these are set by the Helm chart in a real deployment. They are listed
# here so the full surface is visible in one place; leave them unset locally.
#
# REQUIRE_AUTH   Reject any request that did not arrive through an
#                authenticating proxy. Set "true" in every deployed environment
#                — it is what makes a misconfigured ingress fail closed rather
#                than silently publish the whole CDR. Unset locally, where Vite
#                talks to the BFF directly and there is no proxy. (There is no
#                browser SSO locally either — KC_HOSTNAME is pinned in-network —
#                so exercise the identity path with
#                `curl -H 'x-auth-request-user: alice' localhost:3001/api/me`.)
#
# DEFAULT_USER_NAME
#                What lands in `composer|name` when NO proxy identity arrived
#                (local dev only). Deployed, oauth2-proxy always forwards the
#                logged-in user and this is never consulted.
#
# STATIC_DIR     Serve the built SPA from this same process (the container sets
#                /app/dist). Unset locally: Vite serves the SPA and proxies /api.
#
# REQUIRE_AUTH=true
# DEFAULT_USER_NAME=Demo User
# STATIC_DIR=/app/dist

# Used by scripts/seed.ts only.
TEMPLATE_ID=EPS Patient Summary
